Phase-C kit discovery bounds repair
Base: b895f160b19d514ad5b0c2b1e6e66eca146ae992
Branch: senpi-adapter
Date: 2026-08-22

THREAT / ROOT
Cockpit list/find reaches listSenpiSessions, whose baseline Promise.all eagerly opened every candidate while node:readline buffered each header and record through newline. Candidate count therefore multiplied simultaneous attacker-controlled line allocations and CPU.

CONTRACT EVIDENCE
Largest checked fixture header: 172 bytes.
Largest checked fixture record: 67,880 bytes.
Header ceiling: 65,536 bytes (>380x fixture header).
Record ceiling: 16,777,216 bytes (existing jsonl-cursor contract; >240x fixture record).
Default candidate scan concurrency: 4.

RED
- Oversized header test received ordinary JSON parse error instead of code=header-line-too-large.
- Oversized later-record test received ordinary JSON parse error instead of code=record-line-too-large.
- Nine gated parent candidates observed maximum active scans=9; expected 4.

GREEN
pnpm exec vitest run tests/senpi-discovery.test.ts
Test Files 2 passed (2)
Tests 26 passed (26)
Type Errors no errors

MUTATION PROOF
- Replacing workerCount=min(concurrency,item count) with workerCount=item count made the public-parent test fail: observed 9, expected 4. PARENT_POOL_MUTATION_EXPECTED_FAILURE=PASS.
- Replacing the maxLineBytes guard with an unreachable MAX_SAFE_INTEGER guard made both exact oversized tests fail with ordinary parse errors. MUTATION_BYTE_GUARD_EXPECTED_FAILURE=PASS.
- Both mutations were restored before gates.

